        <<set $fish = $fish + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        <<set $mum = $mum + 1>>
    <<endif>>
    {$charname}: *blushed* umm... well... <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
    {$charname}: Blocked me on Grindr. <<if $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
    {$charname}: Fishman. <<if $charname == "Mothperson">>
    {$charname}: What a smile! <<if $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
-> Muscle Mummy <<if $charname != "Muscle Mummy">>
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        <<set $drac = $drac + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        <<set $witch = $witch - 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        <<set $moth = $moth + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        <<set $fish = $fish + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        <<set $mum = $mum + 1>>
    <<endif>>
    {$charname}: Wouldn't mind studying her anatomy. <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
    {$charname}: Queen! <<if $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
    {$charname}: So sweaty. <<if $charname == "Mothperson">>
    {$charname}: So dedicated! I love it! <<if $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
-> The Ghost
    {$charname}: Boo!
You: Thank you for being so honest with me.
You: Now to get to know you even better, I need your help to make a decision.
-> dreams
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        <<set $drac = $drac + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        <<set $witch = $witch + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        <<set $moth = $moth + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        <<set $fish = $fish + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        <<set $mum = $mum - 1>>
    <<endif>>
    You: I keep having this dream that someone steals all my socks and then I turn into a sock and get stolen too but then we are in a kind of Mafia Romance situation where he gives me 365 days to fall in love with him and if I don't he'll let me go and I am just laying there because I am a sock and what am I supposed to do, I have no arms, I have no legs.
    You: And then he keeps calling me babygirl and asking me if I am lost?
    You: I am a sock, of course I am lost?
    You: Anyways, should I just ask him why he stole my socks?
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        {$charname}: I don't think you have to ask.
        {$charname}: There is only one obvious explanation.
        {$charname}: He is secretly a centipede and buying socks is just to expensive for him.
        You: That makes sense.
        {$charname}: Can you maybe describe him for me?
        You: Tall, dark, handsome?
        {$charname}: That could be anyone!
        You: I know.
        You: Umm.. he has a scar on his cheek.
        You: In the form of a banana.
        {$charname}: Left or right cheek?
        You: Umm.. both. They kind of meet in the middle.
        {$charname}: Sounds like Thoralf.
        {$charname}: But he is not a centipede.
        {$charname}: As far as I know.
        You: I think that might be his name.
        {$charname}: I'll send him a bat about this.
        {$charname}: This is outrageous behaviour.
        You: Thank you.
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        {$charname}: Sure.
        {$charname}: But is he like... hot?
        You: If you are into moustaches, I guess?
        {$charname}: Ah, that I am not sure about.
        You: Fair.
        {$charname}: Maybe he's that one centipede I turned into a guy because he kept walking over my book when I tried to read outside.
        You: It seems possible.
        {$charname}: Last I heard of him, he named himself Thoralf and led a life of crime.
        {$charname}: *shakes head* Some centipedes are just not cut out to be human.
        You: That's why they are centipedes.
        {$charname}: Correct.
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        {$charname}: Only if you know that you can stomach the answer.
        You: Huh?
        {$charname}: Sometimes asking questions leads us to things that we would have rather not known.
        They stare into the lämp.
        What do they know?
        What secret forbidden knowledge do they possess?
        {$charname}: But I digress.
        {$charname}: In your dream, what kind of sock are you?
        You: Usually a striped one.
        {$charname}: Yellow and orange?
        You: Yellow and orange.
        {$charname}: Delightful.
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        {$charname}: Should I call you babygirl?
        You: Please don't.
        You: I don't think that's the part of the dream where my subconscious is trying to tell me something.
        {$charname}: As you wish.
        He bows slightly and looks at you in a way that will definitely make in into at least your daydreams.
        And you thought those couldn't get any wetter.
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        {$charname}: Should I beat him up for you?
        You: What?
        {$charname}: I'm sure I could get him to reveal where your socks are.
        {$charname}: Why he took them is irrelevant. 
        {$charname}: Because that is just rude.
        You: If you put it like that.
        You: To be honest I never questioned it.
        {$charname}: Then it is high time you did.
        {$charname}: What a disgusting little man.
        {$charname}: Who does he think he is?
        You let her rant.
        It's endearing.
        And hot and sweaty.
    <<endif>>
-> cats
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        <<set $drac = $drac + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        <<set $witch = $witch + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        <<set $moth = $moth + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        <<set $fish = $fish - 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        <<set $mum = $mum + 1>>
    <<endif>>
    You: Should I get one or two more cats?
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        {$charname}: I am allergic to cats.
        You: Skill issue.
        {$charname}: True.
        You: But what about my cats?
        {$charname}: They make perfect snacks to go. Like little juice boxes.
        You: What?
        {$charname}: What?
        You: Well, should I get one or two?
        {$charname}: If you have to then get two.
        You: That sounds reasonable.
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        {$charname}: Get two.
        You: Huh, that was quick.
        {$charname}: Well you know what they say.
        You: ... no?
        {$charname}: The more pussy, the better, ayyyyyy!
        You: ...
        {$charname}: ...
        You: ...
        {$charname}: Sorry, I guess I am still a bit drunk.
        You: No worries.
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        {$charname}: How many do you already have?
        You: Three.
        {$charname}: And how many lämps?
        You: Umm... 
        You try to count.
        You: Maybe like 12?
        {$charname}: Then have as many cats as you like.
        You: But I don't know how many I would like.
        You: That's why I am asking you.
        {$charname}: Then get one.
        {$charname}: You can still get more later.
        You: That's great advise!
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        {$charname}: I would advise you to get just one.
        {$charname}: Because every cat is a queen.
        {$charname}: And deserves to be treated as such. 
        {$charname}: If you have to many, then you may not have the time to treat all of them the way they deserve.
        He seems uncharacteristically serious for a second.
        It suits him.
        {$charname}: And I know my fair share about treating someone right.
        There's a twinkle in his eyes that might just give you a heart attack.
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        {$charname}: I love cats.
        You: So do I.
        {$charname}: I think you should get two.
        {$charname}: They are just too adorable.
        You: I agree!
        {$charname}: And so soft.
        {$charname}: And cuddly.
        She absentmindedly starts to pet your hair.
        You instinctively start purring.
        You are way too into this.
        {$charname}: I also love Cats.
        You: The musical?
        {$charname}: Definitely not the movie.
    <<endif>>
-> curse
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        <<set $drac = $drac + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        <<set $witch = $witch - 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        <<set $moth = $moth + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        <<set $fish = $fish + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        <<set $mum = $mum + 1>>
    <<endif>>
    You: I think I may have been cursed by a monkey wizard.
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        {$charname}: Which one?
        You: If I just knew that.
        {$charname}: You should really find that out first.
        {$charname}: Then I may be able to help you.
        You: Really?
        {$charname}: I said may be able.
        {$charname}: I promise nothing.
        You: As you should.
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        {$charname}: The banana peels?
        You: The banana peels.
        {$charname}: Well that seems to be a problem.
        You: You don't say?
        {$charname}: I do.
        You: Do you think there's a way out for me?
        {$charname}: I appreciate your faith in me but that is way out of my area of expertise.
        You: Aren't you a wizard??
        {$charname}: First of all, I am a witch, there is a difference even though most people are not aware of it, thank you very much.
        {$charname}: And secondly, I may not look like it, but I am a Technowitch. Nature magic is just not my thing.
        You: Uh, sorry, I didn't know.
        {$charname}: It's fine.
        {$charname}: I am also sorry. I kind of overreacted because I hate to feel useless.
        You: Yeah, I get that.
        {$charname}: I thought you would.
        You: Excuse me?
        {$charname}: I said what I said.
        He grins and you can't really feel mad.
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        {$charname}: Have you tried human sacrifice?
        {$charname}: It's how my ancestors tried to appease the Great Lämp.
        You: Did it work?
        {$charname}: Sometimes?
        You: So it didn't work?
        {$charname}: Like I said, sometimes.
        You: So maybe it would have worked out even without the human sacrifice?
        {$charname}: Maybe.
        {$charname}: But they did burn so brightly.
        You: How do you know that?
        {$charname}: The information was passed down from the ancestors.
        You: ...
        {$charname}: ...
        You: ...
        {$charname}: ...
        You: When was your last human sacrifice?
        {$charname}: Last week.
        You: Will invite me to your next one?
        {$charname}: If you wish to, you will be very welcome.
        You: I cannot wait to appease the Great Lämp.
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        {$charname}: Oh no.
        You: Huh?
        {$charname}: I am so sorry.
        You: What for?
        {$charname}: That might be my ex.
        You: Your what??
        {$charname}: My ex.
        {$charname}: They weren't too happy about me going on this show.
        {$charname}: Disagree with it on principle, I think.
        You: So they cursed me??
        {$charname}: It is possible.
        You: To get back at you?
        {$charname}: No, no, we are still great friends. It was a really amiable break-up.
        {$charname}: I think this is their idea of a joke.
        {$charname}: And a kind of prostest, because as I said they disagree with the concept of reality television on priciple.
        You: Okay...
        You: But can we circle back to the fact that you used to date a monkey wizard.
        {$charname}: A wizard monkey.
        {$charname}: But yes.
        You: Fascinating.
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        {$charname}: Are you sure it's not a wizard monkey?
        You: Is there a difference?
        {$charname}: There most certainly is.
        {$charname}: Monkey wizards are puny little creatures.
        {$charname}: Physique like wizards, brain like monkey.
        {$charname}: Wizard monkeys on the other hand...
        {$charname}: Strong like a monkey and blessed with a wizardly intelligence.
        You: I didn't know!
        {$charname}: Most people don't.
        {$charname}: So which one is it?
        {$charname}: Monkey wizard or wizard monkey?
        You think.
        You: Monkey wizard I guess.
        {$charname}: Then there's nothing you can do.
        She pats your shoulder.
        {$charname}: Just resign to your fate.
        You: I guess you are right.
    <<endif>>
-> bugs
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        <<set $drac = $drac - 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        <<set $witch = $witch + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        <<set $moth = $moth - 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        <<set $fish = $fish + 1>>
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        <<set $mum = $mum + 1>>
    <<endif>>
    You: There are so many bugs in my code! I hate Godot! What should I do?
    <<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
        {$charname}: You have to try harder.
        You: But I can't!
        {$charname}: Yes, you can!
        {$charname}: And you will!
        {$charname}: Or you will be a total embarrassement just like your parents!
        You: Excuse me? 
        {$charname}: I am sorry, were your parents not total losers?
        You: No, you are right they were.
        {$charname}: See.
        {$charname}: But you still have time not to be like them.
        You nod.
        Somehow you feel better?
    <<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
        {$charname}: Maybe you should just give up.
        You: What? No!
        You: You are supposed to encourage me.
        You: Make me want to try and work harder.
        You: So I can grow and evolve.
        You: Spread my wings and learn to fly.
        {$charname}: Or you could just give up.
        You: Never!
        {$charname}: ...
        {$charname}: And they say that reverse psychology doesn't work.
        You glare at him.
        But you still feel a lot better.
    <<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
        {$charname}: Have you tried eating them?
        You: Who?
        {$charname}: The bugs.
        You: I could try?
        {$charname}: Then they won't bother you anymore.
        {$charname}: Just make sure that the other bugs can see you eating their chum.
        {$charname}: Because then you might not need to eat a lot of them.
        {$charname}: They can upset the stomach in great numbers.
        You think about which bug you should eat first.
        But anyways, you are feeling better.
    <<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
        {$charname}: Oooh, I believe in you.
        You: You do?
        {$charname}: Obviously.
        {$charname}: If you are half as smart as you are attractive then you can do anything you set your pretty little mind to.
        You already forgot your question.
        You brain just plays an endless loop of "Oh no! He's hot!".
        But regardless you are vaguely aware of feeling better.
    <<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
        {$charname}: Squash the bugs!
        {$charname}: Make them afraid of you.
        {$charname}: Then you can master anything!
        You: Even Godot?
        {$charname}: Even Godot.
        She pats your shoulder.
        You feel better.
    <<endif>>
You: I really enjoyed our time together.
<<if $charname == "Dr. h.c. Dr. med. Acula">>
    {$charname}: Bet you say that to everyone.
    You: ...
    You: Yes, yes I do.
    {$charname}: I guess that's the point of the show.
    You smile.
    You: Touché.
<<elseif $charname == "Bobo Blocksberg">>
    You: But you have to tell me.
    You: Was there a party after the elimination yesterday?
    You: And why wasn't I invited?
    {$charname}: Well...
    He's avoiding eye-contact.
    {$charname}: You weren't invited because there wasn't a party.
    {$charname}: Just me alone in this room.
    He smiles weakly.
    {$charname}: Pathetic, aren't I?
    You: I don't think so.
    {$charname}: You don't?
    He seems genuinely surprised.
    You: Next time, just tell me and then we can drink alone together.
    {$charname}: I would love that.
<<elseif $charname == "Mothperson">>
    You: Your lämp is really pretty.
    {$charname}: And so are you.
    They blush.
    You blush.
    Both of you are blushing even harder because the other one is blushing.
    You are stuck in a blush loop.
    It's really adorable.
<<elseif $charname == "Fishy McFishface">>
    {$charname}: Well, wasn't that a pleasure?
    You: ...pleasure.
    What are you doing?
    You were just able to form proper sentences a second ago and now his hand has accidentally brushed your thigh and your brain is going haywire again.
    {$charname}: We should do that again sometimes.
    He has the nerve to wink at you and flash a smile so bright it might attract Mothperson.
    You suddenly have difficulty breathing.
    {$charname}: *laughs* Have I taken your breath away?
    You: I...
    You: I...
    You are wheezing.
    He starts to look really concerned.
    You: I have asthma...
    There is too much damn dust in this Villa.
    {$charname}: Where is your medication?
    He jumps up and runs out of the room after you manage to give him the information.
    He's back with your inhaler in the blink of an eye.
    He pats your back while you wait for the meds to work.
    You: Thanks.
    {$charname}: No worries. Can't have you dying on me, can I?
    {$charname}: Not when I have so much I want to do to you... if you want me to.
    He wispers the last sentence in your ear and you feel another asthma attack oncoming.
<<elseif $charname == "Muscle Mummy">>
    {$charname}: I think I should get back to my workout soon.
    You: Oh, don't let me keep you from it!
    {$charname}: No, I really enjoyed this.
    {$charname}: I mean I would be glad to pause my workout for you anytime.
    You: Really?
    She nods.
    This feels like a really big compliment.
    You are not sure how to respond.
    While you are still thinking, she pulls you in a bonecrushing hug.
    Your bones are not breaking but if they were...
    What a way to go.
    She releases you way to soon.
<<endif>>
===